@description REAPER MCP — Model Context Protocol interface (immersive/spatial audio)
@version 1.11.0
@author James Livingston
@provides
  [darwin] reaper_mcp.dylib https://github.com/inseglet-audio/inseglet/releases/download/v$version/reaper_mcp.dylib
@changelog
  Guard release: the ADM, DAMF and Loom export tools can now FAIL TO MEASURE. All three
  used to author a complete deliverable from a render in which every sample of every
  channel was exactly zero, stamping loudness claims that were just the arithmetic image
  of "no samples" (-120 dB RMS, a -70 LUFS floor, 0.0 active fraction). The old
  render_empty guard only caught a render of zero LENGTH.
  *** BREAKING: authoring a deliberately silent master now needs allowSilent:true. ***
  Passing allowSilent reproduces the previous bytes EXACTLY - the escape hatch is the old
  behaviour, verified byte-identical on three fixtures.
  Surface is unchanged at 190 tools / 3 resources / 5 prompts, but THREE TOOLS GAIN ONE
  PARAMETER - a schema change the tool-count triple cannot see.
  The test is exact zero on every sample of every channel, never a threshold: a real 7.1.4
  deliverable with one channel fed has ELEVEN of twelve channels on the same floor triple,
  so a per-channel rule would reject real work. One 1e-9 sample clears the guard. Whether a
  quiet master is too quiet is not this tool's judgement to make, and the -70 floor is
  correct and stays.
  It was never one site: export_damf authored its triad from the same unmeasured render,
  and export_loom_manifest emitted the same floor triple through intentFillLevels /
  intentBedLufs plus a whole-bed expectLufs of -70. Measured pre-fix on all three.
  docs/REFERENCE.md is regenerated: allowSilent had existed in three input schemas and in
  no user-facing document, because the surface gate counts tools, not parameters.
